---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How We Test & Choose Products"
  description="Our testing methodology: how we research, compare, and recommend products at GearCompared. Hands-on testing, real-world use, and honest reviews."
>
  <main class="content">
    <article>
      <header class="article-header">
        <h1>How We Test &amp; Choose Products</h1>
        <p class="article-desc">
          Every recommendation on GearCompared is backed by real research and testing. Here's exactly how we do it.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section class="guide-section">
        <h2>1. We Research</h2>
        <p>
          Before testing anything, we spend hours reading spec sheets, customer reviews, and expert forums. We identify the products real people are buying — not just the ones with the biggest marketing budgets.
        </p>
        <p>
          We look at at least 20-30 products per category and narrow the field to the top 5-8 that deserve a closer look.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="guide-section">
        <h2>2. We Test (or Buy and Use)</h2>
        <p>
          We purchase products at retail price — we don't accept free samples from manufacturers. This keeps our reviews independent. For each product, we use it for at least two weeks of normal daily use before forming an opinion.
        </p>
        <p>
          For standing desks: we assemble them, adjust them, work on them for full workdays, and test stability at standing height.
        </p>
        <p>
          For kitchen appliances: we run them through their paces with real cooking tasks — blending smoothies, air-frying frozen foods, brewing coffee, baking with stand mixers.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="guide-section">
        <h2>3. We Compare (Fairly)</h2>
        <p>
          Every product is scored on the same criteria for its category. We look at:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Performance</strong> — does it do what it promises?</li>
          <li><strong>Build quality</strong> — will it last?</li>
          <li><strong>Value</strong> — is it worth the price?</li>
          <li><strong>Ease of use</strong> — setup, daily operation, cleaning</li>
          <li><strong>Customer satisfaction</strong> — verified Amazon ratings and review trends</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="guide-section">
        <h2>4. We Update</h2>
        <p>
          Prices change. New models launch. Ratings shift. We re-check our picks regularly and update reviews when things change. Every review includes a "last updated" date so you know you're reading current information.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="guide-section">
        <h2>Our Pledge</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>We buy the products we review at retail price</li>
          <li>We never accept payment for placement or reviews</li>
          <li>If a product is bad, we say so</li>
          <li>Commissions never influence our rankings</li>
          <li>We disclose how we make money clearly and prominently</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="guide-section">
        <h2>How We Make Money</h2>
        <p>
          GearCompared earns affiliate commissions when you buy products through our links. This costs you nothing extra. We are a participant in the Amazon Services LLC Associates Program.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="/disclosure/">Read our full affiliate disclosure &rarr;</a>
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
